<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>MP4/4 Telemetry & Development Log</title>
    <!-- Import Google Model Viewer for 3D GLB Rendering -->
    <script type="module" src="https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/model-viewer/3.4.0/model-viewer.min.js"></script>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg-color: #0f1115;
            --card-bg: #181b21;
            --accent-red: #ff1801;
            --text-main: #e6e8ec;
            --text-muted: #8b949e;
            --border-color: #2d3139;
        }

        body {
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
            background-color: var(--bg-color);
            color: var(--text-main);
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        header {
            background-color: var(--card-bg);
            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent-red);
            padding: 2rem 1rem;
            text-align: center;
        }

        header h1 {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 2.2rem;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        header p {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            margin-top: 0.5rem;
            font-style: italic;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 2rem auto;
            padding: 0 1rem;
        }

        .section-title {
            font-size: 1.4rem;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-red);
            padding-left: 0.75rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        }

        /* 3D Model Viewer Box */
        .viewer-container {
            background-color: var(--card-bg);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: 8px;
            overflow: hidden;
            margin-bottom: 3rem;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
        }

        model-viewer {
            width: 100%;
            height: 450px;
            --poster-color: transparent;
        }

        /* Dedication Log Styling */
        .log-entry {
            background-color: var(--card-bg);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 1.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
            transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;
        }

        .log-entry:hover {
            border-color: var(--accent-red);
            transform: translateY(-2px);
        }

        .log-header {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        }

        .log-title {
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            color: #fff;
        }

        .log-meta {
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            color: var(--accent-red);
            font-weight: bold;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        .log-body {
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.95rem;
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 2rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            margin-top: 3rem;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <header>
        <h1>MP4/4 Development Telemetry</h1>
        <p>"No matter what your dream is, you have to dedicate yourself entirely to it." — Ayrton Senna</p>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
        <!-- 3D MODEL VIEWER SECTION -->
        <h2 class="section-title">Interactive 3D Chassis Model</h2>
        <div class="viewer-container">
            <!-- Replace 'car-model.glb' with your actual GLB filename -->
            <model-viewer 
                src="car-model.glb" 
                alt="3D McLaren MP4/4 CAD Model" 
                auto-rotate 
                camera-controls 
                shadow-intensity="1.5"
                exposure="1"
                environment-image="neutral">
            </model-viewer>
        </div>

        <!-- DEDICATION LOG SECTION -->
        <h2 class="section-title">Dedication Log</h2>

        <div class="log-entry">
            <div class="log-header">
                <span class="log-title">Log 01: Concept Initialization & Regulatory Framework</span>
                <span class="log-meta">Week 1 // Completed</span>
            </div>
            <div class="log-body">
                Analyzed the 1988 McLaren MP4/4 architecture to establish our baseline aerodynamic philosophy[cite: 1]. Identified key regulatory rules regarding minimum car mass (30.0g) and wheel dimensions. Formulated team roles across Project Management, Aerodynamics, Webmaster, and Manufacturing.
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="log-entry">
            <div class="log-header">
                <span class="log-title">Log 02: Initial CAD Modeling & Gordon Murray Geometry</span>
                <span class="log-meta">Week 3 // Completed</span>
            </div>
            <div class="log-body">
                Modeled the primary chassis body in browser-based CAD. Dropped the nose cone angle to minimize frontal area and created aggressive sidepod undercuts to channel airflow directly to the rear[cite: 1]. Ran initial mass readouts against the polyurethane foam density baseline[cite: 1].
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="log-entry">
            <div class="log-header">
                <span class="log-title">Log 03: Virtual CFD & Structural Optimization</span>
                <span class="log-meta">Week 5 // Completed</span>
            </div>
            <div class="log-body">
                Generated a high-fidelity rendering model featuring detailed cockpit assembly and classic livery graphics[cite: 1]. To survive launch tube impact while saving weight, engineered low-mass hollow carbon fiber wishbones for the front and rear suspension assemblies.
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="log-entry">
            <div class="log-header">
                <span class="log-title">Log 04: Mass Excavation & Manufacturing Conversion</span>
                <span class="log-meta">Week 7 // Completed</span>
            </div>
            <div class="log-body">
                Created the manufacturing CAD configuration. Closed the open cockpit into a sleek 1.0mm canopy shell and removed non-structural interior geometry[cite: 1]. Shelled the body to a 1.2–1.5mm uniform wall thickness and hollowed floor pockets to lock in our target dry CAD mass of 15.5g.
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="log-entry">
            <div class="log-header">
                <span class="log-title">Log 05: Assembly, Finishing & Final Scrutineering</span>
                <span class="log-meta">Week 9 // Final Calibration</span>
            </div>
            <div class="log-body">
                Applied custom Day-Glo Red and White paint coats with wet-sanding passes. Installed precision low-friction bushings, carbon wishbones, and Goodyear Eagle decals[cite: 1]. Final dry mass verified on digital scales at exactly 30.0g—fully compliant and track-ready.
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>

    <footer>
        &copy; 2026 F1 in Schools Team // Powered by GitHub Pages
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
